---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LivingStrip from '../../components/LivingStrip.astro';
import RiskDecoder from '../../components/RiskDecoder.astro';
import RiskPath from '../../components/RiskPath.astro';
import RiskWatch from '../../components/RiskWatch.astro';
import facts from '../../../docs/risk/six-percent-that-stays.facts.json';
import '../../styles/risk.css';

const title = 'The thirty-year Treasury yield in late August 2026';
const subhead = 'The yield was about 5.21 to 5.26 percent. A hold near 6 percent through a long-term borrowing date is separate from a single morning at that rate.';

const howToRead = 'Usual case is the late-August thirty-year. Named tail is ~6% that lasts through a long-term borrow. Watch is the hold — not a morning print.';

const watchItems = [
  'Whether the thirty-year holds above 5.75 percent, then 6 percent, through a long-term borrowing date, not for a single morning.',
  'How well ten-year and thirty-year auctions clear.',
  'The mortgage spread.',
  'TGA as cash for the week.',
  'Bills vs longer.',
  'Purchases at least $4 billion through early November.',
];
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} — Rycode`}
  description={subhead}
  variant="risk"
>
  <article class="risk-digest">
    <header class="risk-digest-head">
      <h1 class="risk-digest-title">{title}</h1>
      <p class="risk-digest-subhead">{subhead}</p>
      <LivingStrip facts={facts} part="strip" />
    </header>

    <div class="risk-digest-preface">
      <RiskDecoder
        terms={[
          { term: 'Usual case', gloss: 'the late-August thirty-year.' },
          { term: 'Named tail', gloss: '~6% that lasts through a long-term borrow.' },
          { term: 'Watch', gloss: 'the hold — not a morning print.' },
        ]}
        quiet={[
          'Quiet: ~$950B TGA · checking account, week cash — not a purchase program.',
          'Quiet: one-point rise ≈ 0.3% of output first year on debt that comes due.',
        ]}
      />
    </div>

    <div class="risk-digest-columns">
      <div class="risk-digest-main">
        <figure class="risk-path-plate">
          <p class="risk-path-kicker">How it works</p>
          <p class="risk-path-title">Usual case → named tail → watch</p>
          <RiskPath
            title="Usual case, named tail, and watch"
            desc={howToRead}
            stages={[
              { name: 'Usual case', lines: ['late-August thirty-year'] },
              { name: 'Named tail', lines: ['~6% that lasts'] },
              { name: 'Watch', lines: ['hold, not a morning'] },
            ]}
          />
          <figcaption>{howToRead}</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p class="risk-digest-lede">The essay on this site, <a href="/economics/ten-trillion-to-roll/">About $10 trillion of U.S. debt comes due and has to be refinanced</a>, is the story of the number. This page is the risk read of the same facts. It is not a second telling of bills, the checking account, or the four-billion-dollar purchases.</p>

        <section class="risk-digest-section" id="usual" data-digest-section="usual">
          <h2>Usual case</h2>
          <p>The government will replace about ten trillion dollars of debt in the coming year. Most of that is short-term bills it already rolls every week. The thirty-year yield in late August was about 5.21 to 5.26 percent. That is an expensive year. It is not a crash.</p>
          <article class="risk-card risk-card--inline">
            <p class="risk-card-kicker">Usual case</p>
            <p class="risk-card-figure">5.21–5.26%</p>
            <p class="risk-card-label">Thirty-year, late August</p>
            <p class="risk-card-note">Expensive year. Not a crash.</p>
          </article>
        </section>

        <section class="risk-digest-section" id="named-tail" data-digest-section="tail">
          <h2>The named tail</h2>
          <p>The bad outcome that is not the usual case is the thirty-year Treasury yield going to about 6 percent and remaining there through at least one round of long-term borrowing. From late August that is a move of about three-quarters of a percentage point. A single print at 6 percent that fades is not the tail. A 6 percent rate that lasts is.</p>
          <article class="risk-card risk-card--inline">
            <p class="risk-card-kicker">Named tail</p>
            <p class="risk-card-figure">~6%</p>
            <p class="risk-card-label">That stays through ≥1 long-term borrow</p>
            <p class="risk-card-note">~0.75 pt from late August. A single morning print that fades is not the tail.</p>
          </article>
        </section>

        <section class="risk-digest-section" id="related-tails">
          <h2>Related tails, not the same event</h2>
          <p>Do not fold every bad rates story into 6 percent. Auction demand can weaken while the thirty-year is still 5.3 to 5.6. Home-loan spreads can widen so households feel 6 percent mortgage pain before the Treasury is at 6 percent. A failure of bill auctions is a different and more extreme event. It is not the lead.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="risk-digest-section" id="watch" data-digest-section="watch">
          <h2>What to watch</h2>
          <RiskWatch items={watchItems} />
          <article class="risk-card risk-card--inline">
            <p class="risk-card-kicker">Watch</p>
            <p class="risk-card-figure">5.75% → 6%</p>
            <p class="risk-card-label">Hold through a long-term borrow date</p>
            <p class="risk-card-note">Not a single morning. Also: auction clear, mortgage spread, TGA as week cash, bills vs longer, $4B purchases.</p>
          </article>
        </section>

        <LivingStrip facts={facts} part="log" />

        <div class="risk-digest-closer">
          <p class="risk-closer-kicker">From this essay</p>
          <p class="risk-closer-link"><a href="/economics/ten-trillion-to-roll/">About $10 trillion of U.S. debt comes due and has to be refinanced</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="risk-digest-rail" data-digest-rail data-digest-fallback="tail" aria-label="Digest, risk read">
        <p class="risk-digest-kicker">Digest · Risk read</p>
        <div class="risk-digest-viewport">
          <div class="risk-digest-stack">
            <article class="risk-card" id="card-usual" data-card="usual">
              <p class="risk-card-kicker">Usual case</p>
              <p class="risk-card-figure">5.21–5.26%</p>
              <p class="risk-card-label">Thirty-year, late August</p>
              <p class="risk-card-note">Expensive year. Not a crash.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="risk-card" id="card-tail" data-card="tail">
              <p class="risk-card-kicker">Named tail</p>
              <p class="risk-card-figure">~6%</p>
              <p class="risk-card-label">That stays through ≥1 long-term borrow</p>
              <p class="risk-card-note">~0.75 pt from late August. A single morning print that fades is not the tail.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="risk-card" id="card-watch" data-card="watch">
              <p class="risk-card-kicker">Watch</p>
              <p class="risk-card-figure">5.75% → 6%</p>
              <p class="risk-card-label">Hold through a long-term borrow date</p>
              <p class="risk-card-note">Not a single morning. Also: auction clear, mortgage spread, TGA as week cash, bills vs longer, $4B purchases.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script is:inline src="/digest-rail.js" defer></script>
